# Sliding Window Pattern: Revision Notes

## What Is Sliding Window?

Sliding Window is an optimization technique used to process a **contiguous part** of an array or string.

A window represents a range:

```text
[left ........ right]
```

Instead of recalculating every possible subarray or substring from the beginning, we reuse information from the current window.

When the window moves:

```text
1. Add the new right element
2. Remove the old left element when required
3. Update the answer
```

Sliding Window often reduces:

```text
Brute Force: O(n²) or O(n³)
Sliding Window: O(n)
```

