## No Duplicate Characters

```java
while (window.contains(currentCharacter)) {
    window.remove(s.charAt(left));
    left++;
}
```

Used in:

```text
LeetCode 3
```

---

## Sum Reaches Target

```java
while (windowSum >= target) {
    updateMinimumLength();

    windowSum -= nums[left];
    left++;
}
```

Used in:

```text
LeetCode 209
```

---

## At Most `k` Distinct Values

```java
while (frequency.size() > k) {

    int leftValue = nums[left];

    frequency.put(
        leftValue,
        frequency.get(leftValue) - 1
    );

    if (frequency.get(leftValue) == 0) {
        frequency.remove(leftValue);
    }

    left++;
}
```

For Fruit Into Baskets:

```text
k = 2
```

---

## At Most `k` Replacements

```java
while ((right - left + 1) - maxFrequency > k) {
    frequency[s.charAt(left) - 'A']--;
    left++;
}
```

Formula:

```text
Replacements required = Window length - Maximum frequency
```

Used in:

```text
LeetCode 424
```

---

## Frequency Arrays Must Match

```java
if (Arrays.equals(requiredFrequency, windowFrequency)) {
    return true;
}
```

Used in fixed-size permutation and anagram problems.

---

## Window Contains All Required Characters

```java
while (formed == required) {
    updateMinimumWindow();
    removeLeftCharacter();
    left++;
}
```

Used in:

```text
LeetCode 76
```

