# Why Sliding Window Is Usually O(n)

Sliding Window often contains a `for` loop and a nested `while` loop:

```java
for (int right = 0; right < n; right++) {

    while (condition) {
        left++;
    }
}
```

This may look like `O(n²)`, but it is usually `O(n)`.

Why?

```text
right moves from 0 to n - 1 only once.
left moves from 0 to n - 1 only once.
```

Neither pointer moves backward.

Therefore:

```text
Total right movements = at most n
Total left movements  = at most n

Total operations = at most 2n
Time complexity = O(n)
```

