# Universal Maximum-Window Template

```java
int left = 0;
int answer = 0;

for (int right = 0; right < input.length; right++) {

    // Step 1: Include input[right].
    addToWindow(input[right]);

    // Step 2: Restore the window condition.
    while (windowIsInvalid()) {
        removeFromWindow(input[left]);
        left++;
    }

    // Step 3: The window is valid, so update the maximum.
    answer = Math.max(
        answer,
        right - left + 1
    );
}

return answer;
```

---

# Universal Minimum-Window Template

```java
int left = 0;
int answer = Integer.MAX_VALUE;

for (int right = 0; right < input.length; right++) {

    // Step 1: Include input[right].
    addToWindow(input[right]);

    // Step 2: Record and shrink every valid window.
    while (windowIsValid()) {

        answer = Math.min(
            answer,
            right - left + 1
        );

        removeFromWindow(input[left]);
        left++;
    }
}

return answer == Integer.MAX_VALUE ? 0 : answer;
```

---

# Universal Fixed-Window Template

```java
int left = 0;

for (int right = 0; right < input.length; right++) {

    // Step 1: Include input[right].
    addToWindow(input[right]);

    // Step 2: Remove one element if the window is too large.
    if (right - left + 1 > k) {
        removeFromWindow(input[left]);
        left++;
    }

    // Step 3: Process complete windows of size k.
    if (right - left + 1 == k) {
        updateAnswer();
    }
}
```

